                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client had a transsphenoidal resection of the pituitary gland to remove a pituitary tumor. The nurse notes drainage on the nasal dressing. Suspecting cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) leakage, the nurse would look for drainage that is of which characteristic?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nCSF leakage after cranial surgery may be detected by noting drainage that is serosanguineous (from the surgery) and surrounded by an area of clear or straw-colored drainage. The typical appearance of CSF drainage is that of a \"halo.\" The nurse also would further verify actual CSF drainage by testing the drainage for glucose, which would be positive.",
                        "id": "17ee0acf03b54ebe8806038a999a7d43",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "aa4963d577244c35a546a093939e68b8",
                                "content": "Temporal lobe and frontal lobe"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "fd7b6cd1f7e143bca7d27cd09c1648da",
                                "content": "Hippocampus and frontal lobe"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "43c119f4b148427d8b2faf2a197b1edc",
                                "content": "Limbic system and cerebral hemispheres"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "91739e6d8fcb4eababc04cb8bfa27ae1",
                                "content": "Reticular activating system and cerebral hemispheres"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "aa4963d577244c35a546a093939e68b8",
                                    "content": "Temporal lobe and frontal lobe"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "fd7b6cd1f7e143bca7d27cd09c1648da",
                                    "content": "Hippocampus and frontal lobe"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "43c119f4b148427d8b2faf2a197b1edc",
                                    "content": "Limbic system and cerebral hemispheres"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
