                        "content": "The nurse is assessing the client's level of consciousness and documents that the client has delirium. On the basis of this documentation, the nurse would determine that there is damage to which area of the nervous system?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "c2472dbaf30269ec1d4a4af474a31869",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Understanding 理解",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nInsomnia, agitation, mania, and delirium are caused by excessive arousal of the reticular activating system in conjunction with the cerebral hemispheres. The temporal lobe, hippocampus, and frontal lobe are responsible for memory. The limbic system is responsible for feelings and affect.\n",
                        "id": "1842548d261740d1acbf9a8e71ff489c",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
