                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is providing care to a client with increased intracranial pressure (ICP). Which approach is beneficial in controlling the client's ICP?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nNursing interventions to control ICP include maintaining a calm, quiet, and restful environment. Environmental noise would be kept at a minimum. Visiting needs to be monitored to avoid emotional stress and interruption of sleep. Interventions would be spaced out over the shift to minimize the risk of a sustained rise in ICP.",
                        "id": "186f427674884179aaec0e53521ff845",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
